      "math_academy_id": "q-89197",
      "knowledge_point_id": "2669e657-da47-5e22-9ac5-7a69f3b0a55f",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given Algebraically",
      "problem": "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $9{x}^{2}-36{y}^{2}=36?$",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-36{y}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{36{y}^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we $a=\\sqrt{4}=2$ and $b=1.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\n$$",
